<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">On this day</h2><ul class="cen-days"><li><a href="/today-in-history/december-31"><span class="dt">31 December 1600</span><span class="nm">Elizabeth I charters the East India Company</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/february-17"><span class="dt">17 February 1600</span><span class="nm">Giordano Bruno is burned at the stake in Rome</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-21"><span class="dt">21 October 1600</span><span class="nm">Tokugawa Ieyasu wins the Battle of Sekigahara</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/october-6"><span class="dt">6 October 1600</span><span class="nm">Peri's Euridice, the oldest surviving opera, is performed</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/january-1"><span class="dt">1 January 1600</span><span class="nm">Scotland begins its year on 1 January instead of 25 March</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/november-8"><span class="dt">8 November 1602</span><span class="nm">The Bodleian Library opens in Oxford</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/may-15"><span class="dt">15 May 1602</span><span class="nm">Bartholomew Gosnold names Cape Cod</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/march-20"><span class="dt">20 March 1602</span><span class="nm">Dutch East India Company is founded</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/march-24"><span class="dt">24 March 1603</span><span class="nm">Elizabeth I dies and James VI of Scotland inherits England</span></a></li><li><a href="/today-in-history/november-1"><span class="dt">1 November 1604</span><span class="nm">Othello is performed before James I at Whitehall</span></a></li></ul></section>
